{
  "title": "Hyperparathyroidism",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9089/hyperparathyroidism",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 21 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Hyperparathyroidism is the increase in serum parathyroid hormone (PTH) production that may be of primary, secondary or tertiary causes.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made based on evaluation of serum labs and clinical evaluation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment can be medical management or tumor resection depending on underlying cause of disease.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "5",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occurs in **0.1%** of the population",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "90% result form a **single adenoma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "remaining 10% from **parathyroid hyperplasia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common in women",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hyperparathyroidism and malignancy make up the majority of patients with **hypercalcemia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "PTH indirectly stimulates osteoclasts by binding to its receptor on osteoblasts, inducing RANK-L and M-CSF synthesis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Excessive PTH leads to **over-stimulation of bone resorption**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cortical bone affected more than cancellous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Brown tumor**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "resembles a giant cell tumor of bone relating to focal demineralization of bone in the setting of hyperparathyroidism.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Primary",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "typically the result of **hypersecretion of PTH** by a parathyroid **adenoma/hyperplasia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may result in **osteitis fibrosa cystica**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "breakdown of bone, predominently subperiosteal bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "commonly involves the jaw",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Secondary",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "secondary parathyroid hyperplasia as **compensation from hypocalcemia or hyperphosphatemia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "↓ gut Ca2+ absorption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "↑ phosphorous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "associated conditions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**chronic renal disease**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "renal disease causes hypovitaminosis D",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "leads to ↓ Ca2+ absorption",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**renal osteodystrophy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "bone leisons due to secondary hyperparathyroidism",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Tertiary",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**parathyroid glands become dysregulated after secondary hyperparathyroidism**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "secrete PTH regardless of Ca2+ level",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "",
              "table": [
                {
                  "header": true,
                  "cells": [
                    {
                      "colspan": 4,
                      "bullets": [
                        {
